ROLE 1
Data & Platform Engineer
Level: Intermediate to Expert
ROLE SUMMARY
Owns the end-to-end data infrastructure: real-time streaming, Spark/PySpark batch + structured-streaming, Delta Lake storage, the Feature Store, and platform operations. Ensures every transaction, KYC record, and sanctions update flows reliably from source systems into the Feature Store, Delta Lake, and Graph DB where ML models consume them — sub-second latency on the real-time path, daily completeness on the batch path.
RESPONSIBILITIES
•	Real-time ingestion: Kafka (KRaft mode, 3+ brokers, Avro Schema Registry), Flink streaming jobs (now scoped to lightweight on-demand single-batch evaluations triggered by analysts), Debezium CDC connectors from core banking and KYC systems
•	Primary batch & micro-batch pipeline: Spark / PySpark on Delta Lake (MinIO) — feature computation, scoring orchestration, materialisation jobs, partitioned by entity type and date, Delta time-travel for regulatory back-testing
•	Spark Structured Streaming consumers for aml.signal_payloads and downstream Layer-3/Layer-4 topics
•	Airflow DAGs (aml_detection_pipeline and friends): nightly + 4-hourly delta runs, Kafka sensors, REST-triggered ad-hoc runs, backfills, retraining DAGs, sandbox simulations
•	dbt transformations and data-quality tests on Delta tables
•	Feature Store: Feast in on-prem mode, backed by MinIO (offline) + Redis Cluster (online, HSET-based serving); materialisation jobs that push fresh features from Delta into Redis after each batch
•	Dual-mode Feature Factory: daily batch for stable features (KYC, demographics) + real-time/streaming computation for volatile features (velocity, amount clustering)
•	Avro Schema Registry: schema management, backward-compatibility enforcement, data-contract validation across every Kafka topic (aml.txn, aml.kyc, aml.lists, aml.signal_payloads, aml.entity_risk, aml.decisions, …)
•	Coverage Meta-Monitor: auditing 100% of transaction types/channels/products are flowing; dead-letter Delta tables and pipeline-halt logic on schema/contract failures (P4 incident path)
•	Platform infrastructure: on-prem Kubernetes (single cluster, multi-namespace: aml-data, aml-storage, aml-ml, aml-serving, aml-observability, aml-sandbox), Helm charts, ArgoCD / GitOps deployments, CI/CD pipelines, Prometheus + Grafana, ELK (Elasticsearch + Logstash + Kibana) for centralised logging, GPU node provisioning with separate sandbox quotas
REQUIRED SKILLS
•	Apache Kafka — topic design, partitioning, consumer groups, exactly-once, KRaft mode, Avro + Schema Registry
•	Apache Spark / PySpark — batch and Structured Streaming, Delta Lake (ACID, time-travel, schema evolution, OPTIMIZE/Z-ORDER), executor tuning
•	Apache Flink or Kafka Streams — stateful stream processing, windowed aggregations, watermarks, late-event handling
•	CI/CD: Jenkins, GitLab CI, or GitHub Actions; GitOps with ArgoCD for cluster deployments
•	Containerisation: Docker — multi-stage builds, registry management (ECR/Harbor)
•	Apache Airflow — DAG design, sensors (incl. Kafka sensor), REST-trigger patterns, retry/alerting, backfills
•	dbt — incremental models, tests
•	Kubernetes (on-prem) — pods, HPA, Helm, resource quotas, priority classes, GPU scheduling
•	Redis — feature-serving data structures, Cluster mode, TTL, HSET patterns
•	MinIO (S3-compatible) operations — buckets, lifecycle, IAM
•	Infrastructure as Code — Terraform or Pulumi
•	Monitoring — Prometheus, Grafana, ELK (or Loki)
•	Python (compulsory) — NumPy, Pandas, PySpark as the daily working language
NICE TO HAVE
•	Feast or Tecton (Feast on-prem strongly preferred)
•	Debezium CDC configuration
•	Neo4j ETL pipeline experience (graph builder)
•	Cloud-native experience on AWS (EKS, MSK, Kinesis) or GCP (GKE, Pub/Sub, Dataflow) — useful for patterns even though target is on-prem
•	Delta Lake internals; Apache Iceberg or Hudi for comparison
•	ArgoCD / Argo Workflows / Argo Events

ROLE 2
ML Engineer 1
Level: Intermediate to Expert
RESPONSIBILITIES
•	Transaction Neural Network (PyTorch): architecture, training, HPO, inference serving via BentoML (GPU runner pool) — replaces TorchServe as primary serving path; TorchServe/Triton remain acceptable as fallback knowledge
•	Ensemble Model (XGBoost/LightGBM): meta-model fusing NN, GNN, rule, raw signals into a single calibrated score; served from BentoML CPU runner pool with adaptive micro-batching
•	Unsupervised anomaly detection: AE / VAE (PyTorch) or isolation forest for zero-day patterns, drift management, peer-group calibration
•	Multi-axis scoring at Transaction, Account, Client axes before aggregation
•	Signal Aggregator (Layer 3): typology-specific aggregation, Recurrence Engine
•	Dual-track escalation: Track A deterministic + Track B probabilistic ML consolidator
•	5D Tuning Matrix (Country × Client Type × Product × Risk Level × Transaction Profile) — Bayesian smoothing, cold-start inheritance; parameters fetched per-scoring from Redis, sourced from PostgreSQL Global Tuning Matrix
•	Calibration: Platt scaling, score-to-probability mapping, MC Dropout confidence intervals
•	Retraining pipeline as an Airflow DAG with the four mandatory tasks; MLflow model registry managing five lifecycle stages; champion–challenger promotion via GitOps PR merged through ArgoCD
•	BTL active learning, focal loss, SMOTE, stratified mini-batches
•	Sandbox workflow: experiments tracked in Sandbox MLflow, outputs to dedicated Delta Lake partition tagged with simulation_run_id, read-only access to production stores
REQUIRED SKILLS
•	Python (compulsory) — NumPy, Pandas, Scikit-learn, PySpark for feature engineering at scale on Delta Lake
•	PyTorch — architecture, custom losses (focal), training loops, GPU optimisation
•	XGBoost / LightGBM — gradient-boosted trees, feature importance, SHAP
•	MLOps: MLflow (experiment tracking + model registry, lifecycle stages), BentoML (runners, adaptive batching, CPU + GPU pools), A/B / champion–challenger via GitOps + ArgoCD
•	Delta Lake basics — reading/writing partitions, time-travel for back-testing
•	Statistical foundations — class imbalance, calibration theory, hypothesis testing
•	Anomaly detection — autoencoders/VAEs, isolation forests, reconstruction loss, drift detection
•	Model evaluation — PR curves, AUC-ROC, F-beta, lift charts
NICE TO HAVE
•	W&B alongside MLflow (the tech design uses both)
•	Evidently AI or similar drift/monitoring platforms
•	DVC or LakeFS for dataset versioning
•	TorchServe / Triton / KServe (alternative serving paths)
•	Financial-crime / fraud datasets, SHAP/LIME, time-series behavioural features

ROLE 3
ML Engineer 2: Graph & GNN Engineer
Level: Intermediate to Expert
RESPONSIBILITIES
•	Knowledge Graph in Neo4j: schema (entity nodes, transaction edges, ownership, sanctions links, counterparty connections, corporate registry data)
•	Graph ETL: build/maintain graph from raw sources (entity matching, dedup, dirty corporate registry data, incremental updates driven from Spark jobs writing to Delta Lake)
•	Graph Neural Network (PyTorch Geometric) — architecture, message-passing, training on the entity graph, sub-graph extraction for inference; GNN inference served from BentoML GPU runner pool
•	Network-level features: shell-company score, circular flow detection, sanctions proximity (N-hop), shared UBO discovery, community risk, betweenness, PageRank — recomputed weekly via Airflow + Spark + Neo4j
•	Entity Resolution: deterministic + probabilistic + vector-embedding similarity for Customer 360
•	Sub-graph extraction optimisation: k-hop neighbourhood from Neo4j must complete within 200ms for real-time scoring
•	Cypher query optimisation at scale (50M+ nodes, 500M+ edges); the queries Graph RAG generates must execute efficiently
•	Network Axis scoring: 4th evaluation axis — per-entity network risk + node embeddings, written to Delta Lake (aml.entity_risk companion tables) and pushed into Redis online features
REQUIRED SKILLS
•	Python (compulsory) — graph ETL, GNN training, Neo4j Python driver, PySpark for batch graph feature joins
•	Neo4j — Cypher, modelling, indexes, APOC, bulk import
•	PyG or DGL — GCN/GAT/GraphSAGE, mini-batch training, sub-graph sampling
•	Graph algorithms — community detection, centrality, shortest path, cycles, temporal graphs
•	Entity resolution — Jaro-Winkler/Levenshtein, blocking, probabilistic record linkage
•	Data engineering fundamentals — messy data, dedup, incremental ETL on Delta Lake
NICE TO HAVE
•	Corporate registry data (OpenCorporates, Companies House, commercial)
•	AML typologies involving network structures (layering, shell networks, smurfing)
•	TigerGraph or Amazon Neptune
•	Embedding-based entity matching (Sentence-BERT)
•	BentoML packaging for GNN inference


