ROLE 5
Backend & Integration Engineer
Level: Intermediate
ROLE SUMMARY
Owns every backend service that is not an ML model: Alert Service, Case Manager, API Gateway, Tuning Matrix data structure, alert de-dup, Signal Aggregator, rule-engine config, and all external system integrations. Builds the 'last mile' that makes ML outputs usable.
RESPONSIBILITIES
•	Alert Service: score → alert → tier routing → Kafka publish on aml.decisions / downstream topics; dual-track escalation (Track A deterministic + Track B ML consolidator)
•	Case Manager backend: alert lifecycle state machine, SLA tracking, assignment routing — alert objects pushed via Kong API Gateway to the Case Management UI
•	API Gateway: Kong — rate limiting, auth, routing across microservices (Kong is the chosen gateway in the tech design; AWS ALB removed as primary option but acceptable as alternate experience)
•	Tuning Matrix backend: 5D threshold structure, PostgreSQL as system-of-record (Global Tuning Matrix), Redis as low-latency read cache, CRUD API, self-tuning from analyst feedback
•	Alert De-duplication Engine — entity + temporal + transaction overlap, alert merging
•	Signal Aggregator (Layer 3) backend — typology-specific rules, Recurrence Engine, threshold evaluation against the Tuning Matrix
•	Rule Engine integration — Drools or custom Python rule engine, rule config API, versioning
•	Feature Factory API — serving computed features as JSON via FastAPI, on-demand consumption by models and services; backed by Feast / Redis online store
•	Model Config Registry (PostgreSQL) — table mapping each active production model to its scoring path; CRUD + audit
•	External integrations — core banking, KYC, sanctions (OFAC/UN/EU), FinCEN BSA E-Filing API for SAR submission
•	Workforce analytics backend — investigator metrics, skill-based routing, workload balancing, SLA dashboards
•	Audit trail in PostgreSQL + Delta Lake — immutable logging of every score, feature snapshot, model version, decision, and config version
REQUIRED SKILLS
•	Python (FastAPI) — REST design, async, middleware (FastAPI is the standard in the tech design; Node.js/Express acceptable as supplementary)
•	PostgreSQL — schema design, query optimisation, JSONB, migrations, versioned config tables
•	Apache Kafka — Avro + Schema Registry, consumer/producer patterns, exactly-once, DLQs
•	API design — REST conventions, versioning, JWT/OAuth, rate limiting
•	Integration patterns — webhooks, retry with backoff, circuit breakers, idempotency
•	State machine design — alert lifecycle, concurrent access, audit logging
•	Docker — microservice containerisation, docker-compose, Dockerfile optimisation
•	API documentation — OpenAPI / Swagger
•	Kong (or similar API gateway) configuration
•	Redis as a read-side cache for hot config (Tuning Matrix parameters)
NICE TO HAVE
•	Drools or similar BRMS
•	FinCEN BSA E-Filing API experience
•	Event-driven patterns (CQRS, event sourcing)
•	Multi-tenant SaaS backend services
•	GitOps / ArgoCD for service deployment
•	gRPC and Protobuf alongside Avro

ROLE 6
QA & Security Engineer
Level: Intermediate
ROLE SUMMARY
⚑ Can be a shared / on-demand resource initially; becomes critical as the system approaches production and regulatory review. Owns end-to-end QA across the full pipeline, data security and PII compliance, the pre-filing QA engine for SAR quality, and red-team testing.
RESPONSIBILITIES
•	Integration testing: end-to-end traces of a synthetic transaction from ingestion → features → scoring → alert → investigation context — across the full Kafka → Spark → Delta Lake → BentoML → Kong → Case Manager path
•	Regression testing on every model update, rule change, threshold adjustment
•	Red-team simulations of synthetic laundering — structuring, layering, shell networks, same-day attacks, wire stripping — executed in the dedicated aml-sandbox namespace using Sandbox Spark + Sandbox MLflow, with outputs landing in the dedicated Delta Lake simulation_run_id partition
•	Pre-filing QA Engine for SAR completeness, consistency, regulatory compliance, dismissal justification, peer comparison
•	SWIFT Message Integrity Analyzer — comparing payment messages at gateway entry/exit, detecting field stripping, blank originators, resubmission of blocked payments
•	Data security — encryption at rest and in transit, PII handling (GDPR, banking secrecy), RBAC, immutable audit trails in PostgreSQL + Delta Lake
•	Penetration testing coordination
•	Model validation support — test data, bias datasets, benchmarking for SR 11-7
•	Schema-contract testing against the Avro Schema Registry — backward-compatibility gates in CI
•	GitOps PR review gates — quality checks that must pass before ArgoCD promotes a model from Staging → Production
REQUIRED SKILLS
•	Python — pytest, integration test frameworks, synthetic data generation
•	Test architecture — distributed-system E2E testing, test data management, environment management
•	Security fundamentals — AES, TLS, RBAC/ABAC, PII classification, data masking
•	Compliance awareness — GDPR, banking data handling, regulatory examination expectations
•	CI/CD integration — quality gates, automated rollback triggers, ArgoCD-based promotion gates
•	Code quality — SonarQube or similar static analysis
•	Kafka / Avro Schema Registry compatibility testing
•	Basic Spark / Delta Lake to write integration tests against Delta tables and replay-from-time-travel scenarios
NICE TO HAVE
•	SWIFT message formats (MT103, MT202, MT700)
•	Financial-services security frameworks (NIST, ISO 27001)
•	SR 11-7 model risk management
•	Red-team / adversarial testing
•	OWASP ZAP, Snyk, HashiCorp Vault for secrets
•	MLflow model-registry governance and lineage auditing

